<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucus Augusti</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lugo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucus Augusti, modern Lugo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>, north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, was a Roman town founded around 25 BCE. It became a leading centre of Roman Gallaecia and later its provincial capital. In the late 3rd century it was enclosed by walls more than two kilometres long, which survive complete and are a World Heritage Site. It later became a bishopric under the Suebi.</p></div>
